    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T08:05:33Z",
    "body": "Release reproduction on upstream/main 983f527bd confirmed the heavy pin is red. cargo test -p camcraft-app --release --test pocket3d_hsm the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level -- --ignored --exact --nocapture failed at pocket3d_hsm.rs:171. Levels Z 15, 10, 5 and 0 fall back to Offset rings because the plans exceed optimal load.\n\nThe held patch changes only the ignore reason to name #1950 and this cause. It preserves all test bodies and assertions and the three #[test] attributes. A temporary metadata pin failed before the fix, passed after it, failed when the upstream file was restored, and passed when the patch was restored. No goldens changed.\n\nThe quick gate passed. Required clippy failed twice on unchanged crates/app/src/operation/heights.rs:128, .map(&resolve), with needless_borrows_for_generic_args under -D warnings (clippy 1.99.1). That file matches upstream/main exactly. I stopped under step 7 instead of changing unrelated code.\n\nThe uncommitted patch remains on issue/2469-heavy-pin-ignore in .claude/worktrees/issue-2469. Logs remain outside the branch in /tmp/2469-heavy-release-no-cache.txt, /tmp/2469-quick-gate.txt, /tmp/2469-clippy.txt and /tmp/2469-clippy-retry.txt. No PR was opened. Claim released; the issue is free again.\n",
